sec.p:
FRET and NFRET percentage was calculated by subtracting the contributions of CFP and YFP bleed through from the FRET signal using the following:


FRET=IFRET−(BTDonor∗IDonor)−(BTAcceptor∗IAcceptor)NFRET%=(FRET(IAcceptor∗IDonor))∗100
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{gathered}F R E T=I_{F R E T}-\left(B T_{D o n o r} * I_{D o n o r}\right)-\left(B T_{A c c e p t o r} * I_{A c c e p t o r}\right) \\ N F R E T \%=\left(\frac{F R E T}{\sqrt{\left(I_{A c c e p t o r} * I_{D o n o r}\right)}}\right) * 100\end{gathered}$$\end{document}

Scramble and STX11 shRNA transduced, Orai1, Stim1 double knockdown HEK293 cells where were plated on Poly-D-Lysine coated glass bottom dishes (Cellvis) and transfected with 0.5 ug DNA each of Orai1-CFP and Orai1-YPF using Lipofectamine 2000. 16 hours post transfection, co-transfected cells were imaged using PlanApoN 60XO/1.42 NA objective with Olympus FV3000 laser scanning microscope. Images were acquired with the following excitation laser and emission bandwidth parameters using DM405-445/514 dichroic mirror: CFP Ex-405nm Em-460-508nm; YFP Ex-514nm Em-530-630nm, with 4% offset. The pre bleach images of Orai1-CFP (the donor) and Orai1-YFP (the acceptor) were captured, sequentially. This was followed by bleaching of the acceptor, Orai1-YFP, using 100% 514 laser power for 2 mins and then acquiring the donor and acceptor images post bleach. ROIs were drawn around the cell periphery using the Orai1-CFP image. Local thresholding was performed using Bernsen’s algorithm to generate binary masks, which were then applied to the CFP images to measure mean intensities. The background subtracted mean intensities of CFP images were measured for each cell and the FRET efficiencies were calculated as follows:
E%=(1−IbeforeIafter)∗100 \begin{document}$$\displaystyle E \%=\left(1-\frac{I_{\text {before }}}{I_{\text {after }}}\right) * 100$$\end{document}
Ibefore and Iafter denotes the average fluorescence intensity of the donor in the plasma membrane before and after acceptor photobleaching.

Line profiles of Orai1-YFP and BTX-A647 were drawn on raw confocal images of HEK293 cells. Quantifications of Orai1-YFP and BTX-A647 were calculated using the following formula:


%Orai1−YFPorBTX−A647in thePM=(PMIntensityTotal Intensity)∗100
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \% \text { Orai } 1-Y F P \text { or } B T X-A 647 \text { in the } P M=\left(\frac{P M \text { Intensity }}{T \text { otal Intensity }}\right) * 100$$\end{document}
